  "introduced_by": "saurischia",
  "notes": "One 16 m bay of a long stone bridge in the Charles Bridge manner: a pier with rounded cutwaters 11 m across, a segmental arch about 13.5 m wide, an 8 m paved deck between parapets, and over the pier a robed saint of dark stone with a gilt halo on a limestone plinth each side (one holds a cross, one a staff). Chained along a crossing: the anchor is the deck's top at the pier end, the bay runs back along +Z. Hung at the deck's height (base rim).",
